# DomiWEB · restaurants → menu product (always)

For food businesses (restaurantes, cafés, mariscos, beach restaurants, chimis, bars with food), the default deliverable is the **digital menu + QR + WhatsApp ordering** product — not a full marketing website.

## Default funnel

1. Scrape/qualify with restaurant niche config
2. `generate-menus`
3. `claim-pages --product menu`
4. `outreach --product menu` (WhatsApp link = **claim URL only**)
5. `send-whatsapp --product menu` (then `--price` / `--close` as needed)
6. Commit + push `public/menus`, `public/claim`, `public/edit-menu` before first WA

## URLs

- **1:1 outreach / owner link:** always `…/claim/<slug>/` (standard). Never lead with `/menus/<slug>/`.
- **Public / promo share:** `https://tinyurl.com/domenus` (pretty short link → menu-digital splash). Env: `MENU_SHARE_URL`.

## Do not

- Default to `generate-sites` / claim `site` for restaurants
- Treat “claim site” / “create a site” / “scan and claim” for a food place as a website request — ship the **menu** claim instead
- Put the long GitHub Pages menu or splash URL in first-touch WhatsApp or ads — claim for owners, tinyurl.com/domenus for product share
- Invent real dish prices; placeholder items + honesty footer only

## Exception

Use `generate-sites` for a restaurant only when the user explicitly asks for a website (instead of or in addition to the menu).

Talleres / auto repair still use the full `site` funnel.
